    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d609-a1">

                <pb facs="0621" n="587" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg587"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 1268.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Stamford Manufacturing
                            Company to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-04-26"><hi rendition="#small-caps">April</hi> 26,
                        1897</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Marmarak, Greek subject, one of our employees, is forced to leave Alexandretta
                    to-morrow. Forty thousand dollars of our property in his hands unaccounted for.
                    Our two engineers also leave, causing our factory be closed. We regard Ottoman
                    Government responsible for accruing losses.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stamford.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
